

AC(8)                UNIX Programmer's Manual                AC(8)



NAME
     ac - connect-time accounting

SYNOPSIS
     ac [ -w wtmp ] [ -p ] [ -d ] [ people ... ]

DESCRIPTION
     Ac prints the total connect time of each user who has logged
     in during the life of the current /etc/wtmp file, computed
     from the login and logout records it holds.  A grand total is
     printed as well.

     -w wtmp      Read the accounting records from wtmp rather than
                  from /etc/wtmp.

     -p           Print a total for each user (a "per person"
                  report); without it only the grand total is
                  printed.

     -d           Break the report into one midnight-to-midnight
                  period per line.

     Any people arguments restrict the report to the named login
     accounts.

FILES
     /etc/wtmp     the login and logout accounting log

SEE ALSO
     last(1), who(1), w(1), login(1), init(8), utmp(5)

NOTES
     The log /etc/wtmp is written by init(8) and login(3).  Neither
     creates it, so accounting runs only while the file exists;
     that is the switch that turns it on and off.  FGX ships the
     file empty, so accounting is on by default.  Left alone the
     log grows without bound -- there is no cron to roll it over --
     so a site that wants it short collects what it needs and
     truncates or recreates the file.

     Connect time is reported in hours to two decimal places.

FGX                            2.11BSD                           1
